WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.912
Every Transformer has a limit on how much input it can process at once.

00:00:04.912 --> 00:00:09.222
The context window includes more than the user’s latest sentence.

00:00:09.222 --> 00:00:15.352
System instructions, conversation history, examples, retrieved documents, tool results,

00:00:15.352 --> 00:00:21.882
and the tokens reserved for the answer can all compete for the same context budget.

00:00:21.882 --> 00:00:27.842
Long context is useful, but it does not remove the need for good information selection.

00:00:27.842 --> 00:00:33.512
If we simply paste hundreds of pages into a prompt, we may exceed the model limit,

00:00:33.512 --> 00:00:40.012
increase cost and latency, or make it harder for the model to focus on the most relevant evidence.

00:00:40.012 --> 00:00:47.562
Tokenization also matters because context limits are measured in tokens, not pages or words.

00:00:47.562 --> 00:00:53.852
This limitation creates a natural motivation for retrieval: instead of sending every document,

00:00:53.852 --> 00:00:59.010
find the most relevant chunks first and give the model a smaller, focused context.
